<title>USA: Judge sets hearing to probe Prozac case agreement.</title>
<headline>Judge sets hearing to probe Prozac case agreement.</headline>
<byline>Kevin Drawbaugh</byline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Kentucky judge ordered a preliminary hearing scheduled for October 11 to begin investigating an agreement reached in 1994 between Eli Lilly &amp; Co and plaintiffs in a landmark Prozac lawsuit.</p>
<p>Jefferson Circuit Court Judge John Potter said earlier this month that Kentucky Assistant Attorney General Ann Sheadel would lead the investigation.</p>
<p>A spokesman for Indianapolis-based Lilly, manufacturer of the world's top-selling anti-depressant Prozac, said the company is aware of the hearing and declined further comment.</p>
</text>
